From 43806ad740507335eb04556c8c6adc1ec0e6dcd7 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: daveey <daveey@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Fri, 13 Nov 2026 08:11:31 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] [daveey] pm: a borrowing HERMES_HOME runs the owner's
 committed environment

A launch under a HERMES_HOME that borrows the owner's checkout (a test's temporary
home, a per-task home) synced a full environment of its own on every new home,
and `HERMES_HOME=<tmp> hermes --version` refused outright: _METADATA_FLAGS skips
prepare_launch, then activate_dependencies found nothing committed under the
borrower and raised 'no dependency environment is committed'.

- pm.environments.borrowed_venv: the generation the owning root committed for the
  checkout (owner facts.json, read-only; must be a generation of the owner's own state).
- activate_dependencies: on PM's store Python with nothing committed, lease that
  generation in place (a lock file in the owner's <gen>/.leases, the same pin the
  owner's processes take) instead of refusing; no owner generation still refuses.
- pm.install.borrowed_venv_is_current: the owner generation serves the borrower when
  the borrower has no selection of its own and the stamp recomputed for the
  borrower's first-sync request and plugin members equals the owner's stamp.
- venv_sync._prepare_borrowed_launch asks that through a new 'borrowed' launch
  probe operation and skips its own sync when it holds; a borrower with other
  plugins/extras, or no answer, keeps syncing its own.

Never writes the owner's facts or inputs stamps.
